sg-office-editors (8.2.0.143+sg3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Saving a copy as PDF (File > Download as, Print to PDF) no longer
    marks the document saved: the window closed without asking and the
    change was lost (QA: typed text gone from the .docx). The PDF is a
    copy; the document stays as modified as it was.
  * File > Print prints: a PDF of the document (x2t) goes to the printer
    chosen in the print dialog through CUPS (lp), with the editor's pages,
    copies and sides; Quick Print uses the default printer; Print to File
    writes the PDF. It did nothing before.
  * CSV files open (they failed with "An error has occurred while opening
    the file"): the engine is told the encoding (UTF-8, UTF-16 by mark,
    else Windows-1252) and the delimiter (comma, semicolon or tab, as the
    file uses most); a CSV is saved back with its own delimiter. Plain
    text files get their encoding too.
  * The font tables (allfontsgen, ~27 s on the QA VM) are made only when
    the fonts change (fontconfig's list fingerprinted), not at every start;
    meanwhile a window says SG Office is getting ready.
  * One SG Office: a later start hands its files to the one running (a
    socket in the session's runtime directory) and leaves -- a second
    document opens in a second window at once, and a file already open
    brings its window forward instead of opening twice.
  * File > New, Open, Open Recent and Close work (they did nothing); the
    recent files are kept (~/.local/share/sg-office/recent.json).
  * After Save As the editor's title is the new file name.
  * Alt+F4 closes the window, Ctrl+W the document.
  * The windows have SG Office's icons (drawn by the program), the title
    bar too, and so do their taskbar buttons: each program's window has
    its own X class (sg-office-documents, -spreadsheets, -presentations;
    no spaces -- the compositor's list ends a class at one), and the
    program writes the matching .ico files into the Wine profile's
    "Linux app icons" folder the taskbar reads (wine-sg 0612).
  * The title bar's close cross is drawn pixel by pixel like its
    neighbours: antialiased, it was a faint grey two pixels wide.
  * The editors take a document as a local file (offline), as the
    ONLYOFFICE desktop editors do: they decided by file:// and ours come
    from sgoffice://, so they offered chat, mail merge and version history
    and showed "All changes saved" in the status bar while the document
    was still unsaved.
  * Closing a changed document asks Save, Don't Save or Cancel.
  * Open and Save As list the account's folders (Desktop, Documents,
    Downloads, Pictures, Music, Videos) under its home, as File Explorer's
    Quick access does; the dialogs open in the details view.
  * A US English account measures in inches (Office's default there), and
    the editors take the account's language and region.
  * Settings > Colors' dark mode: the editors' dark theme, a dark title bar
    and dark dialogs, following a change while running.
  * Gates: test/app/features_check.py (csv, export, print, fonts, altf4,
    units, title, handoff, dark, recents), each with a mutant
    (make test-app-mutation: bridge noprint/notitle/online, program
    SG_MUTANT_FONTS_EVERY_START/CSV_NO_PARAMS/EXPORT_SAVES/NO_ALTF4/
    UNITS_CM/NO_HANDOFF/NO_DARK/NO_RECENTS/NO_TASKBAR_ICON/FAINT_CLOSE/
    NO_PLACES).

 -- Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>  Thu, 01 Oct 2026 17:45:00 +0000

sg-office-editors (8.2.0.143+sg2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The editors' "new feature" tips (Spreadsheets' "Updated Pivot Tables"
    on every start) are marked seen: build/assemble-app.sh lists the tips
    this build of the editors has (sg-seen-tips.js), and editor.html marks
    them in the editors' storage before an editor loads. Test: make test-deb
    (the list is in the package; mutant "tips": test-deb-mutation). VM: the
    tip on every start with +sg1, never with this build.
  * The build writes no Python bytecode into the tree: the package gate's
    tests ran in a user namespace and left __pycache__ owned by its uids,
    which dh_clean could not remove -- the next release's package build
    stopped.

