sg-office-editors (8.2.0.143+sg1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First package: SG Office, Stained Glass OS's office suite based on
    ONLYOFFICE 8.2.0.143 (sdkjs, core, web-apps), built from source by
    `make deb` -- the program /usr/bin/sg-office, the engine in
    /usr/lib/sg-office/engine, the editors in /usr/share/sg-office. Replaces
    the LibreOffice-based interim suite (sg-shell's sg-office now depends on
    this package). Test: make test-deb (the built package installed into a
    scratch system root, its contents and dependencies checked, the program
    gate run as installed; mutants: no ONLYOFFICE credit, a missing
    dependency, a moved engine, a converter that cannot run).
  * The program opens the rest of the types the shell registers for it
    (.dotm, .dot, .xltm, .xlsb, .xlt, .ppsm, .pps, .potm, .pot; saved under
    another name, like .doc), and an empty file -- File Explorer's New >
    Document -- as a new document saved back to that file.

